WHAT RWKV-8's CUDA ACTUALLY IS, since the file names invite the wrong guess.  It is
the SAME wind_backstepping RWKV-7 WKV as RWKV-v5/cuda/wkv7_*, in fp32 instead of
bf16.  `diff` against the RWKV-v7 copy is three lines in the .cu and one in the
.cpp, all of them the scalar typedef:

    RWKV-v7                                     RWKV-v8
    using bf = __nv_bfloat16;                   using bf = float;
    ...to_float(const bf& u){return __bfloat162float(u);}   { return u; }
    ...to_bf(const float& u){return __float2bfloat16_rn(u);} { return u; }

The difference is upstream's, not ours; both copies are vendored so the diff can be
read here rather than taken on trust.

RWKV-8 = RWKV-7 + ROSA.  ROSA (Rapid Online Suffix Automaton) is what is NEW in
RWKV-8, and the archive ships NO CUDA for it -- ROSA is pure Python in every
RWKV-v8/*.py file.  So this directory is the whole of RWKV-8's CUDA, and the ROSA
half lives in baselines/rwkv_v8/upstream/.  See that directory's PROVENANCE for what
that costs.
